class:: StereoWidth
summary:: Side energy as a normalized stereo width measure
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Amplitude

description::
With M=(L+R)/2 and S=(L-R)/2, returns sqrt(sum(S.squared)/(sum(M.squared)+sum(S.squared))). Identical channels give zero, equal uncorrelated channels approach sqrt(0.5), and inverted channels give one. This is an M/S energy measure; it does not estimate a perceived source angle.

Uses an exact rolling sample window, with output held at zero until it is full. The update cost is linear in the input block size, with a once-per-window sum rebase to bound roundoff drift. Memory is two windows of doubles, allocated at initialization. Formulas are independently implemented from energy, M/S decomposition, and Pearson correlation. Silence returns zero.

Vanilla Amplitude can track channel levels separately; this UGen directly relates the channels over a fixed shared interval.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: left
Left audio-rate input.

argument:: right
Right audio-rate input.

argument:: windowTime
Initialization-time rolling window, 0.001..2 seconds; default 0.05.

returns::
Width from zero through one.

examples::
StereoWidth computes the normalized side-channel energy ratio from an M/S decomposition (0 for mono, ~0.7 for uncorrelated stereo, 1 for fully out-of-phase audio). In this example, measured stereo width dynamically controls the Side channel gain in a Mid/Side matrix: narrow mixes are gently widened, while overly wide or phasey signals are reined in to preserve center clarity. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.stereo:: displays the stereo width ellipse.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("stereo.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 3);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = if(~mir2Buffer.isKindOf(Buffer) and: { ~mir2Buffer.numChannels >= 2 }) {
            PlayBuf.ar(2, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) {
                var sig = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1);
                [sig, DelayC.ar(sig, 0.02, 0.003)]
            } {
                // Synthetic stereo fallback
                var l = Saw.ar(220) * 0.2 + PinkNoise.ar(0.1);
                var r = Saw.ar(222) * 0.2 + PinkNoise.ar(0.1);
                [l, r]
            }
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar([0, 1]);

        var width = StereoWidth.kr(source[0], source[1], windowTime: 0.05);
        var widthLag = width.lag(0.08);
        var mid = (source[0] + source[1]) * 0.5;
        var side = (source[0] - source[1]) * 0.5;
        // Dynamically boost side when width is low, attenuate when width is high
        var sideGain = widthLag.linlin(0.1, 0.7, 1.4, 0.7).clip(0.5, 1.8);
        var enhanced = [mid + (side * sideGain), mid - (side * sideGain)] * 0.25;

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, [0.0, widthLag * 2, 1.0]) };
        enhanced * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.stereo("Stereo Width", ~mir2Bus);
});
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

